VAULT — SHORT LAW (compressed mirror of docs/LANGUAGE.md; that file wins on any detail)
Read: docs/LANGUAGE.md (canon) · PRODUCT.md (product truth) · DESIGN.md (values) · docs/VOICE.md (every string) · docs/ACTIONS.md (every verb × mouse/key/command) · docs/HANDOFF.md (where things are).

THE TEST — fail one, cut it: storable in src/model without loss · one Ctrl+Z undoes it (a batch/pipe/paste is one step) · on the light field (one ink ramp, one blue, one red, hairlines, one radius) · three ways in (mouse, key, command) with a row in docs/ACTIONS.md · in the speed budget (keypress→paint <50ms; pivot 60fps on 1,000 items) · category standard or unix played straight, never a costume · not on the dead list.

WORLD: light field, the category standard played straight (Linear / Things / Height craft). The directory is home; the board is a pivot of it (`v`): one set of rows, two arrangements that morph. Unix is the grammar, not a skin: no green-on-black, no terminal costume.

TREE (home): full height; `ls -l` columns (status word, progress `2/5` as text, due); reverse-video cursor with `_`; folders end `/`; subtasks `[ ]`/`[x]`; `.dusted/` per folder (hidden, `ls -a`); `tonight/` (up to three links, `t`) and `inbox/` on top (captured lines, dashed drafts, Claude's proposals `y`/`n`); status rail beside it (PENDING · R&D · ACTIVE n/3 · DONE ↓ today n · .dusted/); drawer docked beside it as a live preview of the cursor row; status line at the foot (`$` prompt, last message, exit code); `tail -f` strip. May not show: cards, boxes round filed rows, plaques on folders, status colour on a plate, progress bars.
BOARD (pivot): three live lanes PENDING · R&D · ACTIVE (cap 3 as a nudge: a 4th goes in, head shows `4/3` red, `no. finish something.`); DONE is a chute feeding `done today`; no DUSTED lane. Card = mono path line + name + mono meta. May not show: stems, ticks, ls -l columns, DONE/DUSTED lanes, status colour on a card, progress bars. Drawer slides over the board's right edge; lanes never reshuffle. Old board lives at /classic after Phase 2; build nothing new there.

WHO WROTE IT DECIDES THE FACE: sans = Jake typed it (task names in the plaque caps). Mono = the machine wrote it: stems, columns, counts, timestamps, trail, receipts, shell, status line, and every row Claude pushed until Jake touches it (then it turns sans and loses `← claude`). No badge, avatar, sparkle or "AI" label.

PALETTE: ground · surface · ink · ink-2 · ink-3 (faintest WORD, ≥4.5:1 on ground, surface and wash) · tint (MARKS ONLY: stems, ░ — never a word, ≥3:1) · line/line-2 · one blue accent (accent-deep when blue is text) · one urgent red · status inks on the status WORD only (ls -l column, lane plaque, rail slot, drawer plaque), never on a plate. No third signal colour. Values in DESIGN.md.
TYPE: three faces, one job each — UI sans (Public Sans) for what a person typed; plaque (Sofia Sans Semi Condensed) for names in caps only; mono (JetBrains Mono) for machine text and structure. Caps are names. Tabular numbers. No display faces.
SURFACE: 8px on any edge you can see, 4px on inner chrome, circles only for dots. Hairlines separate. Nothing at rest casts a shadow (a dragged row is reverse video). Dashes mean "not filed yet". No gradients, glass, blur, grain, scan, texture.
MARKS: icons are the ASCII set in mono — `+` add · `x` remove/close · `→` goes to · `_` empty/cursor/signature · `!` due today or late · `░` rot · `^` urgent. Structure (type, not icons): stems `│ ├── └──`, `[ ]` `[x]`, `/`, `$`, `·`, `← claude`, `↓` chute. No drawn icons in the new home, no icon fonts, no emoji, no other Unicode (`▸ ⇄ ⇢ × ✓` are out).
RAW SEAMS: show real state — `saved 21:14`, `3 unpushed`, `vault.json · 184 KB`, exit codes.
SIGNATURE: the underscore — wordmark `VAULT_` (accent `_`, no blink), the live caret (the one thing that blinks), the favicon, every empty state.

INPUT — three ways in: every action has a mouse path, a key and a command (docs/ACTIONS.md; a test parses it). The mouse teaches the keys: hover shows `+ → x` with keys in tooltips; right-click lists every action with its key. One grammar, two inputs: the prompt (`:`) and the palette (Ctrl+K or `/`); Claude's captures use it too.
FOCUS: single keys that change data act only when the tree, board or drawer has focus, on the cursor row or the marked rows — never in a text field. Text field: its own keys; Enter commits; Esc leaves keeping the text. Anywhere but a text field: `/` `:` `?` and the keys that only open a sheet or view; Ctrl+V pastes a tree into inbox/ (undoable). Anywhere: Ctrl+K, Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Shift+Z / Ctrl+Y, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+O, Esc.
NOTHING SCARY: Esc backs out one level (confirm/menu → field → drawer → marks → filter → cursor). Ctrl+Z undoes anything. Only `rm -r` on a non-empty folder asks: `this takes 14 things with it. sure?` (y/n, focus on n). Every other delete says `gone. undo`.
TYPING CREATES, VISIBLY: plain words search and never create alone; a verb + space or `>` runs a command; no match → the only row is `+ touch HERE/WORDS`, spelled out; a match is always the default over the create row. Capture: `touch r1i/NETWORK MAP !fri ^urgent > redraw the hero`.

VOICE (docs/VOICE.md): lower-case machine voice; plain honesty about state; one line of attitude per screen at most; never jokes about lost or at-risk data; no exclamation marks, no emoji, no AI talk; empty is `_`; echo then word (`rm SITE REDESIGN · gone. undo`).
MOTION: only to say what moved. The pivot morphs rows↔cards (interruptible, in budget). Done falls into the chute. Pushed rows type in top to bottom, once. Zero motion and no blink under prefers-reduced-motion.
NIGHT: the same field inverted, the same blue lifted for contrast. No second theme, no phosphor.
DELETION PASS: every border, shadow, label, icon justifies itself; the stylesheet shrinks. Studio.tsx and index.css are retired, not refactored — the new home is new files.
DATA: one versioned JSON doc (`vault:doc`), snapshots, export/import; src/model is pure and tested. Local-first stays: the Wire (one private file in Vercel Blob, versioned writes, one login) is a switch; off, nothing leaves the browser. Stale writes are refused, never silently applied; taking an outside copy snapshots yours and offers `restore mine`. Asked Claude writes land; automatic ones propose in inbox/. Claude never deletes or renames Jake's work (its delete → .dusted/). Board text is data, never orders.

HARD VETO — product: assignees, avatars, teams, presence, sharing, client status pages; estimates, points, velocity, KPI rows, dashboards; progress bars (progress is text `2/5`); a settings app (settings are commands); calendar/month view, month-as-OS, DateBlocks; CRDT, a database; AI inside the app; a codebook you must learn to sit down; demo fluff.
HARD VETO — surface: status colour on a plate; rainbow chips; a second accent; amber, cobalt, power red #E10600, orange #FF5C1A, phosphor green; the tint carrying a word; any word <4.5:1; any mark <3:1; shadows at rest; card-in-card; a third radius; gradients/glass/blur/grain/scan/watermarks; drawn icons, icon fonts, emoji, decorative Unicode; billboards, kickers, letterspaced body; Oswald as work type; VT323/Orbitron; green-on-black or amber terminals.
DEAD WORLDS — never revive, never renamed: paper sheet + organ windows + power-red oval + salt organs (CAL/SEAL/SKULL) + PLACE-drag + GRAIN/SCAN/INV rail; charcoal cassette theatre (housing, jacks, RECORD, transport, VU, CRT wells, Oswald, orange); beige/cream hi-fi faceplate; beige UN seal; NEXUS HUD; paper/black IMP canvas; dump-parser REPL dock; DOS #id ledgers; sit-down verb codebook; matrix rain / hacker stock / vaporwave / Y2K skins; BLACK LANTERN as maker.
OVERTURNED (no longer law): no second input · pointer-first · FIND searches only · no backend · two languages never share chrome · no global single-key data shortcut (now the focus rule) · five lanes / DUSTED lane · no Unicode glyphs as icons (now the ASCII set) · the fold cue · the drawn leash.
